# Firebase configuration files (contain sensitive information)
# Not google-services.json / GoogleService-Info.plist: this app applies the
# com.google.gms.google-services Gradle plugin, which fails the Android build
# when the json is absent, and six of the eight Xcode projects list the plist in
# their Resources build phase. Both files hold the same identifiers as
# lib/firebase_options.dart and ship inside the app, so excluding them hid
# nothing and cost two apps their copy (kawaii and letswashlet, 2026-09-02).
# Not firebase_options.dart: the build needs it, and every value in it
# (apiKey, appId, projectId, messagingSenderId, storageBucket, and the
# iOS/Android client ids) ships inside the app binary, so hiding the file
# hides nothing from anyone who has the app. A Firebase API key identifies
# the project; it does not authorize access. Firestore rules and App Check
# do that.
# Not *.plist: that swept up ios/Flutter/AppFrameworkInfo.plist, which Flutter
# needs to build and which carries no app specific values. Name the ones to hide.

# --- Tooling config that belongs to the workspace, not to this app ---
.claude/
.cursorignore

# --- Flutter iOS build output (SPM checkouts, generated env) ---
ios/Flutter/ephemeral/

# --- Build output and generated plugin registrants (regenerated by pub get) ---
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
ios/.symlinks/
ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
ios/build/
ios/Flutter/Generated.xcconfig
ios/Flutter/flutter_export_environment.sh
**/GeneratedPluginRegistrant.*
**/generated_plugin_registrant.*
**/xcuserdata/

# --- Signing assets (added 2026-09-06) ---
# None of these are in any repository today. The rules exist so that a
# certificate exported to the project directory for a one-off cannot be
# committed by a later `git add -A`. Distribution certificates and the App
# Store Connect key grant publishing rights, and a leak is not fixed by
# deleting the file: the history keeps it.
*.p12
*.p8
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
*.jks
*.keystore
